{{USTV|1996}}
The '''1996–97 daytime network television schedule''' for the six major English-language commercial broadcast networks in the United States covers the weekday and weekend daytime hours from September 1996 to August 1997. The schedule is followed by a [[#By network|list per network]] of returning series, new series, and series canceled after the [[1995–96 United States network television schedule (daytime)|1995–96 season]].

Affiliates fill time periods not occupied by network programs with local or syndicated programming. [[PBS]] – which offers daytime programming through a children's program block, branded as PTV at the time – is not included, as its member television stations have local flexibility over most of their schedules and broadcast times for network shows may vary.

==Legend==
{{Plainlist|
* {{Color box|#FFFF66|border=darkgray}} Light yellow indicates talk shows.
* {{Color box|#7fff00|border=darkgray}} Green indicates soap operas.
* {{Color box|#ffc0cb|border=darkgray}} Pink indicates game shows.
* {{Color box|#ffd700|border=darkgray}} Gold indicates news and public affairs programming.
* {{Color box|#99ccff|border=darkgray}} Light teal indicates sporting events.
* {{Color box|#ffffff|border=darkgray}} White indicates local programming.
* {{Color box|#bf9fef|border=darkgray}} Light purple indicates children's and/or [[Regulations on children's television programming in the United States|E/I-compliant]] programming.
* {{Color box|#C0C0C0|border=darkgray}} Gray indicates encore programming (e.g., reruns of prime-time programming).
* {{Color box|aquamarine|border=darkgray}} White with red border indicates other programs not applicable to the above categorizations.
}}
* New series are highlighted in '''bold'''.

==Schedule==
* All times correspond to [[Eastern Time Zone|U.S. Eastern]] and [[Pacific Time Zone|Pacific Time]] scheduling (except for some live sports or events). Except where affiliates slot certain programs outside their network-dictated timeslots, subtract one hour for [[Central Time Zone|Central]], [[Mountain Time Zone|Mountain]], [[Alaska Time Zone|Alaska]], and [[Hawaii–Aleutian Time Zone|Hawaii-Aleutian]] times.
* Local schedules may differ, as [[network affiliate|affiliates]] have the option to pre-empt or delay network programs.<ref>[http://tv.yahoo.com/listings - TV listings - Yahoo.com]</ref> Such scheduling may be limited to preemptions caused by local or national breaking news or weather coverage (which may force stations to tape delay certain programs in overnight timeslots or defer them to a [[sister station|co-operated]] or contracted station in their regular timeslot) and any major sports events scheduled to air in a weekday timeslot (mainly during major holidays). Stations may air shows at other times at their preference.

